# Default API origin for production builds.
#
# Vite loads this file automatically for `vite build`, so a fresh fork or a
# brand new Cloudflare Pages project builds with no dashboard setup. A real
# environment variable (Pages dashboard, CI, or render.yaml) still wins:
# Vite's dotenv loading never overwrites a variable already in process.env.
#
# Why the default lives here instead of only in the dashboard:
# frontend/vite.config.ts fails the build when VITE_API_BASE_URL is unset.
# That guard is deliberate -- without it a wrong host ships a bundle where
# every API call fails while the build stays green. But requiring a manual
# console step made the build unreproducible: it broke on every new Pages
# project, every re-fork, and every fresh clone. This file keeps the
# guarantee while making the build self-contained.
#
# The build still fails if this file is deleted or the variable is unset,
# so the guard keeps its teeth.
#
# For a fork: this points at the upstream Render host, so the fork's frontend
# shares one set of demo data with the original project. Point it at your own
# backend, or set VITE_API_BASE_URL in the Pages dashboard to override it.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://sih-2026-1-n10c.onrender.com